  "id": "f02f817b-5d04-4bb9-9dea-8f65a63d1d30",
  "title": "US F-35 F22 Deal with Saudi Arabia Sparks Controversy Amid Intelligence Concerns",
  "summary": "The U.S. has moved ahead with the sale of F-35 warplanes to Saudi Arabia, despite intelligence concerns about potential technology theft or conflict with China. The deal, initially planned to be a peaceful and strategic agreement, faces challenges due to ongoing tensions and regional security threats.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Saudi Arabia has lobbied the U.S. for years to buy F-35s, the world's most advanced fighter jet.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "U.S. intelligence agencies have warned in internal reports that China could acquire or steal U.S. warplane technology if F-35 jets are sent to Saudi Arabia.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The deal comes as Iran-backed Houthis escalate attacks on Saudi Arabia and seek control of the strategic Strait of Hormuz.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
